<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 263 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 263 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 263 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.3 BLN    1.3 BLN    1.3 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    470 MLN!   970 MLN!   1.233 BLN  =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   81 MLN*     50 MLN*    86 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS	  =     450 MLN*   127 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  T-BILLS	     =	     =     50 MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 389 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING NOVEMBER 6 5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p>(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
